# Scoped deliberately. `core.autocrlf` is true on this machine and there is no repo-wide EOL
# policy here on purpose - do not add `* text=auto` without a separate, measured pass, because
# it renormalises every tracked file at once.
#
# The git hooks are the one place where line endings are load-bearing: sh cannot execute a
# script whose shebang ends in CR, so a CRLF checkout of .githooks/pre-commit breaks committing
# for anyone who clones this repo on Windows.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
